### 🟢 Create a new customer
POST http://localhost:8080/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ricardo",
  "email": "ricardo.mello@mongodb.com",
  "accountNumber": "555",
  "phone": "21000",
  "address": {
    "street": "Street 001",
    "city": "BH"
  }
}

### Retrieve all customers
GET http://localhost:8080/customers

### Find a customer by email (using query parameter)
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/search?email=joao.silva@mongodb.com

### Get total number of customers grouped by city
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/report/total-by-city

### Update the phone number of a customer (by email)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/customers/joao.silva@mongodb.com/phone?phone=4444

### Delete a customer by email
DELETE http://localhost:8080/customers/joao.silva@mongodb.com

### Explain indexes on diagnostics route
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/diagnostics/indexes

### A1. Customer 1001 exists
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/search?email=joao.silva@email.com

### A2. WITHOUT @Transactional, fail after the delete - expect HTTP 500
POST http://localhost:8080/customers/1001/without-transaction?failBeforeRecreating=true

### A4. Put customer 1001 back so part B starts from the same state
POST http://localhost:8080/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "João Silva",
  "email": "joao.silva@email.com",
  "accountNumber": "1001",
  "phone": "1199990001",
  "address": {
    "street": "Rua das Flores",
    "city": "São Paulo"
  }
}

### B1. WITH @Transactional, same failure - expect HTTP 500
POST http://localhost:8080/customers/1001/with-transaction?failBeforeRecreating=true